WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:08.725
<v Audio Description>Visual scene one: Card one highlights in amber while rose sparks flash across the boundary gap between three otherwise healthy cyan system spheres.

2
00:00:09.065 --> 00:00:15.411
<v Presenter>First, most big computer failures happen at the handoffs between teams or parts, not inside them.

3
00:00:15.751 --> 00:00:24.155
<v Audio Description>Visual scene two: Card two turns cyan as an unlabeled amber arrow crosses a boundary seam, illustrating an unwritten unit assumption.

4
00:00:24.495 --> 00:00:29.728
<v Presenter>Second, the cause is usually a guess nobody wrote down, like which units a number uses.

5
00:00:30.068 --> 00:00:37.747
<v Audio Description>Visual scene three: Card three glows emerald as crisp emerald contract rings lock every boundary handoff into stable alignment.

6
00:00:38.087 --> 00:00:44.341
<v Presenter>Third, when every handoff guess is written down and machine-checked, a fix in one place stays fixed.
